{\b\fs22 Terms of use}\par
\par
Stream Assistant Bridge is free software under the MIT License (below). These terms explain what it is meant for; they do not restrict the licence.\par
\par
{\b Intended use.} The bridge is meant for a home or office network: it connects Stream Decks on this computer to a Home Assistant instance in the same local network. Using it from outside the local network (port forwarding of port 5390, exposure to the internet, reverse proxies) is not intended and at your own risk. The bridge refuses connections from public addresses unless it is started with --allow-public true. A VPN into your own network counts as the local network.\par
\par
{\b Your responsibility.} You decide which Home Assistant actions the keys run. Check that a press of the wrong key cannot cause harm, and protect sensitive actions (locks, alarm systems, garage doors) in Home Assistant itself. Keep the pairing code to yourself and keep the software up to date.\par
\par
{\b No warranty, no liability.} The software is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. As far as the law allows, the authors are not liable for any damage that results from installing or using it, from errors in it, or from its use outside the intended purpose. You use it at your own risk.\par
